; XSparkFlow - XAUUSD M30 CandleFlow with the full trailing stack
;
; The same entry rule as xauusd-m30-candleflow.set, with every trailing layer
; turned on. This is a STARTING POINT for optimisation, not a validated profile:
; CandleFlow has never been backtested, forward-tested or traded, and these
; numbers were chosen for plausibility, not measured. Nothing here is a
; profitability claim.
;
; THE TRAILING STACK, from loosest to tightest. On each closed candle every
; enabled layer proposes a stop and the MOST PROTECTIVE one wins; the result is
; then never allowed closer to the market than the floor, and never allowed to
; move backwards.
;
;   Candle anchor   always on: the far wick of the last closed candle, plus the
;                   buffer. Tightest in a steady grind.
;   Chandelier      3.0 x average range below the highest high the trade has
;                   seen (above the lowest low, for a short). This is what stops
;                   one narrow candle from parking the stop under the market and
;                   ending a trend trade early.
;   Tiering         from +1R the 3.0 multiple shrinks linearly, reaching 1.5 at
;                   +4R. A young trade gets room; a mature one gets protection.
;   Breakeven       once the trade has been +1.2R in front, the stop never sits
;                   worse than entry + 0.1R, which covers the spread.
;   Floor           the stop is never closer than 0.35 x average range to the
;                   market, whichever layer proposed it.
;
; TUNING NOTES
; - Widen InpFlowTrailATRMult if the Tester shows trades ending while the move
;   continued. Tighten it if open profit is routinely handed back.
; - InpFlowTrailTightenStartR / FullR is where most of the edge will be, if
;   there is any: it decides how long a winner is allowed to breathe.
; - Raising InpFlowBreakevenAtR reduces the number of scratched trades but
;   leaves more of them exposed to a full stop.
; - The floor must stay above your broker's typical spread in ATR terms, or the
;   stop is inside the noise it is meant to survive.
;
; TO CHANGE TIMEFRAME: attach the EA to a different chart period. Every distance
; here is a multiple of that period's own average range or of the trade's own
; initial risk, so nothing in this file needs editing.
;
; Trading is DISABLED. Turn InpFlowEnableTrading on only after a Strategy Tester
; run and a demo account have shown you what this actually does.

InpFlowEnableTrading=false
InpFlowAutoTuneForSymbol=true
InpFlowMaxOpenTrades=1

InpFlowBufferATRMult=0.10
InpFlowBufferRangePct=0.0
InpFlowBufferPoints=0.0
InpFlowMinStopATRMult=0.25
InpFlowMaxStopATRMult=0.0
InpFlowMinBodyATRMult=0.0

InpFlowMinTrailATRMult=0.35
InpFlowTrailATRMult=3.0
InpFlowTrailTightATRMult=1.5
InpFlowTrailTightenStartR=1.0
InpFlowTrailTightenFullR=4.0
InpFlowBreakevenAtR=1.2
InpFlowBreakevenOffsetR=0.1

InpFlowRiskPct=1.0
InpFlowMaxRiskPct=3.5
InpFlowMaxAccountRiskPct=6.0
InpFlowMaxDailyDDPct=15.0
InpFlowUseTotalDDKillSwitch=true
InpFlowMaxTotalDDPct=25.0

InpFlowUseWeekendClose=true
InpFlowWeekendCloseHour=20
InpFlowWeekendCloseMinute=0

InpFlowVerboseLog=false

InpFlowUseVolatilityGate=false

InpFlowQuietMarketPct=60.0
InpFlowWildMarketPct=600.0
InpFlowEntrySlipPct=25.0
InpFlowExitSlipPct=85.0
InpFlowSpreadCapPct=40.0
InpFlowMaxSpreadATRPct=10.0

InpFlowUseSpreadFilter=true
InpFlowUseStopLevelValidation=true
InpFlowUseMarginCheck=true
InpFlowMarginBufferPct=20.0
InpFlowMaxQuoteAgeSeconds=15

InpFlowMagicNumber=770332
InpFlowOrderComment=CandleFlow_v1
InpFlowClearKillswitchLatch=false
